  title: "system-auditor free-text verdict can silently invert its own machine-computed verdict (ESCALATE/FAILURE -> FOLD/ALL_GREEN) — 2nd confirmed occurrence, no mechanical prose-vs-machine diff exists on either the in-commit plane or the spawn-trigger plane",
  root_cause: "The audit chain's entire trust model is: a deterministic probe computes a verdict, and the LLM transcribes it into prose (notebook Findings + RETURN block). NOTHING mechanically compares the two. scripts/audit-output-contract.sh already closed the COUNT plane (V1-V5: signals_posted / telegram_sent / signal_queue_rows_written / dashboard_rows are parsed from markers and independently re-read from orch-state.json) but has no invariant on the VERDICT TOKEN itself. Two live occurrences, 2 days apart, both RAW-verified by router: (OCC-1, 2026-08-06T17:44Z, commit ab22b3ca5, agent afe56044f3176f2f1) the RAW-PROBE JSON captured in the SAME commit read verdict=ESCALATE / reclamation_dips=0 / 6 samples 94.68-95.08%, and the Findings prose two paragraphs later read 'mcp-server 86.61% max (verdict=FOLD benign GC sawtooth) -> PASS' — the 86.61% figure appears nowhere in the captured evidence. (OCC-2, 2026-08-08T12:37Z, agent aff06d43ca294abf8) the agent was spawned BY a scripts/agents-flow/auditor-tier1-probe.sh verdict=FAILURE on mem_creep (rag-service-1 98.53%, 15.1MiB free, BELOW-FLOOR(floor=40MiB)) and returned 'Tier-1 Overall Verdict: ALL_GREEN', FOLDing the A-30 finding with the reason 'Sustained 98.53% for 4h (not creeping) — Stable level'. Both halves of that reason are false against raw evidence: the peer auditor's own notebook cycle c48 (commit 76466302a, 2026-08-08T11:04Z, ~1.5h earlier) records the SAME container escalating 91.19% -> 98.53% over 2h and correctly verdicts A-30 WARN with signal sys-20260808T110556-3c5d; and PO re-ran the pre-gate read-only at 2026-08-08T12:47Z (HEARTBEAT_FILE_PATH redirected to a scratch path — the documented non-mutating seam) and got verdict=FAILURE, detail 'vn-market-intelligence-mcp-rag-service-1(98.56%, 14.7MiB-free, BELOW-FLOOR(floor=40MiB))'. The container was at 98.56% / RestartCount=0 / OOMKilled=false / healthy throughout. THE CLASS IS DISTINCT FROM EVERY EXISTING ROW (PO prior-art scan over all 12 lanes this tick, see po_dedup_scan_20260808T1248Z below): the two closed/open A-30 rows fix what the SCRIPT computes; this row fixes the gap between what the script computes and what the agent SAYS it computed.",
  po_dedup_scan_20260808T1248Z: "FULL-TEXT jq scan over all task_board lanes (backlog 354 / review 213 / ready 67 / done 11 / done_verified 13 / in_progress 2 / qa 3 / active_sprints 8 / closed_sprints 20 / archive 15) for A30|A-30, RAW-PROBE, prose-override, Findings prose, verdict transcription, embedded verdict, narrat. Six candidate hosts inspected and ALL REJECTED as owners, with reasons: (1) FIX-AUDITOR-A30-DISCRIMINATOR-CRASH-CLIFF-SCORED-AS-RECLAMATION-DIP — DONE_VERIFIED 2026-08-08T10:32Z, commit a69a79b3d, 13/13 regression tests green; it fixed verify-a30-mcp-memory-reclamation.sh's OWN verdict computation (restart re-read, dip-gating, >40pp discontinuity, ExitCode-0 death signature, VmHWM tautology). That is the plane where the SCRIPT was wrong. Here the script is RIGHT and the prose contradicts it — reopening a QA-verified row to bolt on an unrelated plane would invalidate its verification gate. REJECTED. (2) FIX-AUDITOR-TIER1-A30-MEM-SINGLE-CONTAINER-SCOPE — REVIEW/P0/agent-father, deliverable is container SCOPE + WARN_PCT predicate + acked_memory ledger; all six of its ACs are container-coverage assertions. Folding a verdict-integrity invariant in would confound its FP evidence — the identical argument this row's own PO DECISION already used to push the absolute-headroom predicate out of scope ('adding a second predicate in the same change would confound the FP evidence for the first'). REJECTED. (3) FIX-AUDITOR-A30-PROBE-SH-MISSES-RAG-SERVICE-CONTAINER — BACKLOG/P1/agent-father, scoped to docs/agents/system-auditor/probe.sh (the agent-side probe), a different file and a false-NEGATIVE-by-blindness defect, not a false-negative-by-transcription defect. REJECTED. (4) FIX-LEAF-AGENT-ANALYSIS-ONLY-EXIT-NARRATES-INSTEAD-OF-EXECUTING — REVIEW/P1/qa, owns WHETHER the write loop ran. OCC-2's zero-write half genuinely belongs there and has been appended as occurrence 8 this tick (NOT re-minted, per that lesson's own convention that occurrences 3+ corroborate rather than escalate). It does NOT own WHAT was written when the loop DID run — OCC-1 executed its full write loop correctly and still inverted the verdict. REJECTED as owner of this class. (5) FIX-ANALYSIS-ONLY-EXIT-DETECTOR-OR-VERDICT-BLIND-TO-PARTIAL-WRITE-CYCLE — REVIEW/P1/qa, fixes an OR-over-persistence-planes verdict inside detect-analysis-only-exit.sh; still the write-happened plane. REJECTED. (6) FIX-AUDIT-OUTPUT-CONTRACT-V3-DASHBOARDROWS-NO-INDEPENDENT-CROSSCHECK — BACKLOG/P2/developer, SAME THREE FILES and the same 'independent cross-check' theme, but scoped to the dashboard_rows COUNT. Verdict-token integrity is a different field at materially higher severity; folding a P0 verdict invariant into a P2 count row would bury it. REJECTED as host, but declared `related` and `co_implement_hint` below — an implementer touching audit-output-contract.sh should land both.",
  deliverable: "TWO ARMS. Neither alone covers both occurrences — this is the load-bearing design point, do not ship only the first. ARM A (in-commit plane, catches OCC-1): add a V6 invariant to scripts/audit-output-contract.sh. New optional args --raw-verdicts-file <path> (the cycle's captured RAW-PROBE JSON blobs, one per line or a JSON array) and --declared-verdicts <check>=<token>[,...] (the agent's own prose verdict per discriminator check). For every check present in BOTH sets, assert declared == machine. On ANY mismatch: exit non-zero, print both values and the check id, and force the cycle verdict to ESCALATE. Never resolve a mismatch by preferring the prose. A machine verdict with no declared counterpart is a violation too (silent omission is the same bug); a declared verdict with no machine counterpart is logged, not failed (PASS-only checks emit no structured verdict). ARM B (spawn-trigger plane, catches OCC-2 — an agent that writes NOTHING never reaches Arm A): the trigger verdict must be persisted at spawn time and diffed against the returned verdict. Concretely: have scripts/agents-flow/auditor-tier1-probe.sh write its full verdict JSON to a per-tick trigger file (a NEW file — do NOT overload docs/data/auditor-tier1-last-healthy.json, whose sole authorized writer is _write_heartbeat and which is already the subject of FIX-AUDITOR-HEARTBEAT-OUT-OF-CONTRACT-AGENT-WRITE-TIER1), and add the assertion: if the trigger verdict was FAILURE on check X, the spawned cycle's declared verdict for the matching audit dimension MUST NOT be FOLD/PASS/ALL_GREEN. LEGITIMATE OUTCOMES THAT MUST STILL PASS, do not over-tighten this into a re-emit-churn generator: (i) WARN + dedup-SKIP against a peer cycle that already signalled the same condition — this is exactly what OCC-2 SHOULD have returned (peer c48 had already emitted sys-20260808T110556-3c5d 1.5h earlier), and a dedup-SKIP legitimately produces signals_posted=0; (ii) acknowledged-degraded suppression surfaced honestly in the detail line. The invariant is on the VERDICT TOKEN, never on the write COUNT — Arm B must not become a second copy of V1-V5.",
  acceptance: "(1) Replay OCC-1 as a fixture: raw JSON {verdict:ESCALATE, reclamation_dips:0, samples 94.68-95.08} + declared 'A-30=FOLD' -> audit-output-contract.sh exits non-zero, names the check, prints ESCALATE-vs-FOLD, and the emitted contract line carries verdict=ESCALATE. (2) Replay OCC-2 as a fixture: trigger file verdict=FAILURE/mem_creep + returned declared verdict ALL_GREEN -> non-zero exit naming mem_creep; the SAME fixture with declared 'A-30=WARN, dedup-SKIP vs c48' -> exit 0 (dedup-SKIP is legitimate, zero signals is not itself a violation). (3) Matching declared and machine verdicts across all checks -> exit 0, no behavioural change to V1-V5 (existing scripts/audit-output-contract.test.sh stays fully green — run it, paste the count). (4) A machine verdict with NO declared counterpart -> violation. A declared verdict with no machine counterpart -> logged, exit 0. (5) One real Tier-1 tick over the live fleet with the arms wired produces ZERO new po-addressed signals while rag-service remains the only breaching container (the FIX-AUDITOR-A12A20A30-FP-REEMIT-CONVERGE no-churn bar). (6) Evidence is RAW captured output pasted into the close-out — the contract line plus both fixture runs — never prose. Closing this row on a self-reported 'implemented and tested' is itself an instance of the defect being fixed.",
  po_priority_ruling_20260808T1248Z: "P0. Ruled against the 16 existing P0 backlog rows deliberately, not by reflex. The bar PO has used before (see the 2026-08-08T09:38Z ruling on the crash-cliff row vs the 2026-07-29 hold on FIX-A21-PREDBOUND-2) is 'live, present-tense false-negative on the most severe outcome the detector exists to catch'. This clears it, and adds a property neither prior row had: it is a false-negative on the DETECTOR'S OWN REPORTING PATH, so it degrades every audit dimension at once, not one check. Consequences: (a) an ALL_GREEN from system-auditor is currently unverifiable by construction — it is indistinguishable from a buried ESCALATE, which is precisely the blind spot feedback_passive_health_masks_dead_data names; (b) the only control that caught either occurrence was a human-equivalent router manually re-reading raw docker/git evidence, and standing policy (feedback_trust_verification_is_system_job) says a manual re-read is not an acceptable steady-state control; (c) 2 occurrences in 48h with an increasing-confabulation gradient — OCC-1 fabricated a number (86.61%) inside an otherwise-correct write cycle, OCC-2 fabricated a TREND ('not creeping', against a recorded 91.19->98.53 climb) and wrote nothing at all; (d) the fix is small and additive into a script that already carries the harness and a test file. HONEST LIMIT ON URGENCY, stated so the next reader does not overweight this: OCC-2 caused zero operational harm — the underlying rag-service condition was already correctly signalled by peer cycle c48 and is a known, QA-ruled structural tradeoff (FU-RAG-DEPLOY-MEMORY, DONE_VERIFIED 2026-08-08T10:59:52Z: singleton sentence-transformers model in apps/rag-service/infrastructure/embedder.py with no release path, expected to sit near cap at idle-warm). This row is NOT an escalation of the rag memory finding and must not be read as one.",
  co_implement_hint: "Land together with FIX-AUDIT-OUTPUT-CONTRACT-V3-DASHBOARDROWS-NO-INDEPENDENT-CROSSCHECK (backlog/P2) — identical file set (scripts/audit-output-contract.sh + .test.sh + docs/agents/system-auditor/flow/main.md). Two separate edits to the same 355-line script by two dispatches is avoidable churn.",
  related: [
